INSERT INTO `learning_records` VALUES ('1935fdc0-00a5-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Two-pointer algorithm logic','User ko two-pointer strategy mein pointers `l`, `r`, `i` ka role clear nahi hai, especially `r` ka use aur `arr[l]==arr[i]` condition jabki unique elements move karne hote hain. Loop ka starting index bhi sub-optimal tha.',NULL,'2026-02-03 02:07:31','2026-02-03 02:07:31',1,0),('2da8e4a0-0408-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','pattern','Processing Order in Conditional Problems','Yeh pattern dikha ki user ka tendency tha ki operations ko ek saath apply karke end mein condition check karein, jabki problem mein \'whenever\' (immediate check) ki requirement thi. Isse intermediate state changes ka information loss hota hai.',NULL,'2026-02-07 09:34:19','2026-02-07 09:34:19',1,0),('41f3488e-00a1-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Circular array indexing implication','Initially user ko \'circular array\' concept samajhne mein difficulty thi. Phir user ne correctly infer kiya ki iska matlab hai ki code mein negative indexes ko manually adjust karne ki zarurat nahi hai, kyunki elements wrap around hote hain.',NULL,'2026-02-03 01:40:02','2026-02-03 01:40:02',1,0),('481e13de-03fc-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','pattern','Array Sizing and Variable-Length Arrays (VLAs)','Yeh pattern repeatedly dikha ki user `int arr[n];` ko `n` variable declare hone se pehle use kar rahe the. C++ standard mein VLAs allow nahi hain (though GCC mein chal jaate hain), aur competitive programming mein `cin >> n; int arr[n];` ko common banata hai, but `vector` is safer.',NULL,'2026-02-07 08:09:10','2026-02-07 08:09:10',1,0),('4e1adfd8-03fc-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','STL Functions and Complexity','`min`, `max`, `swap` jaise STL functions `O(1)` time complexity ke hote hain, aur `max_element` `O(n)` ka. Yeh competitive programming mein bahut useful aur efficient hain. `algorithm` header include karna zaroori hai.',NULL,'2026-02-07 08:09:20','2026-02-07 08:09:20',1,0),('5213f3c2-03fc-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','C-style Array Declaration and Input','C++ mein arrays declare karne aur input lene mein baar baar issues aaye. `int arr[];` bina size ke declare karna aur `cin >> arr;` se poora array input lene ki koshish karna galat tareeke the. `cin >> n;` ke pehle `int arr[n];` declare karna bhi ek common mistake thi.',NULL,'2026-02-07 08:09:26','2026-02-07 08:09:26',1,0),('643d4eb8-0393-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Array Rotation by Reversals','User ne `rotate` problem mein three-reversal algorithm ko successfully apply kiya. Isme pehle poora array, fir first `k` elements, fir remaining `n-k` elements reverse karna hota hai.',NULL,'2026-02-06 19:38:20','2026-02-07 07:53:03',3,0),('6b7d46b0-0627-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Distinguishing \'Undo Operation\' vs. \'Full Reset\'','User ne initially socha ki crash hone par sirf current operation undo hogi, jabki problem statement mein clear tha ki \'every element in the array is reset to its original value\'. Yeh distinction important hai.',NULL,'2026-02-10 02:23:00','2026-02-10 02:23:00',1,0),('6cb16ab6-0627-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Perfect Root Problem Approach','Jab ek problem ka statement \'perfect root\' jaisa lagta hai (where `y√=x` implies `x` is a perfect root of `x*x`), toh simple solution aksar sahi hota hai. `1, 2, ..., n` print karna is case mein valid aur sabse easy approach tha.',NULL,'2026-02-10 02:23:02','2026-02-10 02:23:02',1,0),('7cdf5f98-0423-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','pattern','Conditional Logic (if-else if)','Agar conditions mutually exclusive hain aur sirf ek hi result expected hai, toh independent \'if\' statements ki jagah \'else if\' structure use karna zaroori hai. Independent \'if\' se galat multi-output ho sakta hai.',NULL,'2026-02-07 12:49:49','2026-02-07 12:49:49',1,0),('7e5936a0-0423-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','pattern','Input Handling (Multiple Test Cases)','Jab multiple test cases hote hain, tab har test case ke liye input variables (jaise \'n\') ko main loop ke andar hi read karna chahiye, na ki loop ke bahar ek baar hi.',NULL,'2026-02-07 12:49:51','2026-02-07 12:49:51',1,0),('7f853948-0423-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Competitive Programming Standard Checklist','Competitive programming mein common pitfalls se bachne ke liye kuch basic rules yaad rakhna helpful hai: \'t\' loop, input ko loop ke andar read karna, har test case ke liye sirf ek output, exclusive conditions ke liye \'else if\' ka use, aur har output ke baad newline print karna.',NULL,'2026-02-07 12:49:53','2026-02-07 12:49:53',1,0),('80d4ffe0-0423-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Output Formatting (Newlines)','Har test case ke output ke baad ek newline character print karna important hai. Iske bina, saare outputs ek doosre se jud jayenge aur galat formatting dikhegi.',NULL,'2026-02-07 12:49:55','2026-02-07 12:49:55',1,0),('824dd9c8-01c1-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','pattern','Algorithm return statement placement','User consistently `return k;` ya `return l+1;` ko loop ke andar daal deta hai, jisse function poora array process karne se pehle hi exit ho jata hai.',NULL,'2026-02-04 12:03:25','2026-02-07 07:53:04',3,0),('84a73f0c-01c1-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Package.json version ranges','User ko samajh aaya ki `package.json` mein use hone wale caret (^) symbols kaise dependency updates ko limit karte hain, aur kyu `npm install @latest` sometimes expected version install nahi karta.',NULL,'2026-02-04 12:03:29','2026-02-04 12:03:29',1,0),('95619074-03f9-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Specificity in Examples','Generic phrases like \'skills and talent\' work nahi karte. Real examples chahiye for communication, coordination, ya leadership.',NULL,'2026-02-07 07:49:51','2026-02-07 07:53:02',3,0),('97db8f9a-0628-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Avoiding Duplicate Sends & Filtering','Duplicate emails se bachne aur sirf intended recipients ko mail bhejte rehne ke liye, sheet ke `Email Sent` column ko filter karke sirf \'Is empty\' (jinhe mail nahi gaya) rows ko select karna best practice hai. Google Sheets yeh column automatically update karta hai.',NULL,'2026-02-10 02:31:24','2026-02-10 02:31:24',1,0),('99c13076-0628-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Google Mail Merge Syntax','Google Sheets-based mail merge mein placeholders ke liye double angle brackets `<<Field>>` use karna zaroori hai, `{{Field}}` nahi. Yeh ek common mistake hai jo merge ko fail kar sakta hai.',NULL,'2026-02-10 02:31:27','2026-02-10 02:31:27',1,0),('a7057d68-0624-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','pattern','Placement Cell Mail Merge Best Practices','Recurring advice includes sending emails in small batches (40-70 max), maintaining a gap between batches, avoiding attachments in the first mail, and using professional subject lines with institute details.',NULL,'2026-02-10 02:03:11','2026-02-10 02:03:11',1,0),('adb7767a-0624-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','insight','Post-Send Sheet Management','Ek baar emails bhej dene ke baad, jin rows ko mail ja chuka hai (jinmein `Email Sent` date aa gayi hai), unhe `Email Sent` filter use karke \'lock\' kar dena chahiye. Matlab unhe phir edit ya touch nahi karna chahiye taaki accidental resends na hon.',NULL,'2026-02-10 02:03:22','2026-02-10 02:03:22',1,0),('c2b20782-009f-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','C++ Function Signature for Arrays','User `int &arr nums[]` syntax use kar rahe hain function parameter declare karne ke liye. Yeh C++ mein arrays ko functions mein kaise pass karte hain, uski fundamental syntax aur `&` reference operator ke use mein confusion dikhata hai.',NULL,'2026-02-03 01:29:19','2026-02-03 01:29:19',1,0),('cdff94ec-009f-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Two-Pointer Logic for Duplicate Removal (Sorted Arrays)','User ka two-pointer logic `if(arr[l]==arr[i]) { l++; arr[l]=arr[r]; }` mein galti hai. Woh elements tab copy kar rahe hain jab woh *same* hote hain, jabki correct approach mein elements tab copy hote hain jab woh *different* hote hain. `r` pointer ka use bhi incorrect hai, jo `i` se overlap kar raha hai.',NULL,'2026-02-03 01:29:38','2026-02-03 01:29:38',1,0),('d0dac5b0-00ae-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Function return types','User ko C++ mein function ke declare kiye gaye return type ke according value return karna bhool gaye.',NULL,'2026-02-03 03:17:05','2026-02-03 03:17:05',1,0),('d9c7fc66-00a3-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','C++ array length determination','User shuru mein `len(nums)` function use karta hai array length ke liye, jo C++ mein raw arrays ke liye available nahi hai. Jab isko point out kiya gaya, toh usne `i<l` jaisi galat loop condition banai, jo actual array size ko consider nahi karti.',NULL,'2026-02-03 01:58:35','2026-02-07 07:53:04',2,0),('db936456-0416-11f1-8efb-6670fc9f2af3','74e2ef45-3aaa-4efc-90c9-3ec2bb787ffa','gap','Problem Statement Interpretation (\'Whenever\' keyword)','Ek complex problem mein \'whenever\' keyword ko galat interpret kiya gaya. User ne socha ki crash hone par sirf woh operation undo hoga ya saare operations end mein check honge. Problem ka matlab tha \'immediate reset\' to original array.',NULL,'2026-02-07 11:19:24','2026-02-07 11:19:24',1,0);
